      sayEn: '“Don’t weary yourself to be rich; in your wisdom, show restraint” (23:4); the moment you fix your eyes on wealth, it sprouts wings like an eagle and flies away (23:5).',
      meanZh: '这不是说赚钱是错的，而是警告那种“耗尽自己去追钱”的心态。财富极其容易流失——它像鹰一样说飞就飞。把人生的重心押在这样一件靠不住的东西上，是不智的。智慧懂得节制，也懂得财富不该成为人活着的终极目标。',
      meanEn: 'This isn’t saying earning money is wrong; it warns against the mindset of exhausting yourself chasing it. Wealth slips away with startling ease — it flies off like an eagle. Staking the center of your life on something that unreliable is unwise. Wisdom knows restraint, and knows that wealth was never meant to be the ultimate goal of living.',
      forMeZh: '我有没有为“多一点”而耗尽自己——牺牲健康、家庭、与神的关系？如果钱明天就飞走，我此刻的奔忙还值得吗？',
