      sayEn: '“Don’t let your heart envy sinners, but rather fear the LORD all day long” (23:17); for surely there is a future hope, and your hope will not be cut off (23:18); so listen, be wise, and keep your heart on the right path (23:19).',
      meanZh: '看着不义的人似乎过得更潇洒、更成功，是一种真实的试探——它会悄悄侵蚀我们走正路的决心。这段话给出的解药不是咬牙硬撑，而是把眼光转向神：终日敬畏他，记得结局还没到，公义的善报和不灭的指望，属于那些持守正道的人。',
      meanEn: 'Watching those who cut corners seem to live more freely and succeed more is a genuine temptation — it quietly erodes our resolve to walk the right road. The remedy here isn’t gritted-teeth willpower but a redirected gaze: fear the LORD all day long, and remember the story isn’t over. A just reward and an unbreakable hope belong to those who hold the right path.',
      forMeZh: '最近我有没有嫉妒那些“走捷径却过得更好”的人？我能不能把眼光从他们身上，转回到“终日敬畏神”和那不致断绝的指望上？',
      forMeEn: 'Have I been envying those who “cut corners and seem to do better”? Can I turn my gaze from them back to fearing God all day and the hope that will not be cut off?',
