      sayEn: 'Who has woe, sorrow, strife, needless wounds, bloodshot eyes? The one who lingers over wine (23:29–30). It goes down smoothly, but in the end bites like a snake (23:31–32); it warps perception until a person doesn’t even feel the blows, yet wakes up wanting more (23:33–35).',
      meanZh: '这是全本《箴言》中对成瘾最写实的描绘。它没有轻描淡写，而是诚实地展示了一个循环：起初的舒畅、逐渐失去的清醒、连痛都麻木的沉沦、以及那句令人心碎的“我几时清醒，我仍去寻酒”。这幅画像不只针对酒，也照见任何一步步夺走我们自由的欲望。',
      meanEn: 'This is the most realistic depiction of addiction in all of Proverbs. It doesn’t soften anything; it honestly shows the cycle: the initial pleasant glow, the slow loss of clarity, the numbness that no longer feels the pain, and the heartbreaking line, “When will I wake up? I will look for more.” The portrait isn’t only about wine; it exposes any desire that strips away our freedom step by step.',
      forMeZh: '我生活中有没有一样东西，正沿着这条曲线——起初是享受，如今开始替我做决定？承认它，是走向自由的第一步；我可以今天就求助。',
